/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * wfsBusReset
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * wfsBusReset()
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * None
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (void) Returns 'void' and hence has no STATUS value
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Resets the VME bus
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * This routine resets the VME bus. It may be used to free up the VME bus if it
 * has hung up after a software or hardware problem. The reset will cause the
 * IOC to reboot.  A pause of 4 seconds has been inserted so that the message
 * that the system is about to reboot will be logged.
 *
 * NOTE:
 * This code has been copied from sysextLib, since sysextLib is no longer going
 * to be used. It only works on an mv167.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * gnirsReboot
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * gnirsReboot()
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * None
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Reboots the system
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Spawns a task which will reboot the system.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
