/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * valid
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * valid(who, where)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) who (int)        which mechanism
 * (>) where (char *)   the position to which we desire to move the mechanism
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Validate a request for positioning from the EPICS layer
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Given a mechanism number, look up the 'where' string in the list of
 * permitted positions in the linked list associated with this mechanism.
 * The valid positions are listed in the configuration files and will have
 * been read and parsed during intialization.  If 'who'
 * is less than zero, prints a bit of diagnostic help.  For the 'filter'
 * "mechanism", looks up the filter pair.  The routine then sets the
 * desired operation as a move to the requested position.
 *
 * For the grating, only determines which grating in use, but not the
 * grating position.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * setGratingTilt
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * setGratingTilt(angle)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) angle (double)
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Set grating to a specified angle.
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Sets a particular angle to which grating shall move when
 * moveAll() is called.  Assumes grating order is equal to one.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * setGratingRot
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * setGratingRot(theta)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) theta (double)       Rotation angle to move grating turret to.
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Grating rotation to encoder position
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Not really needed as a separate function, but perhaps useful this way
 * for testing.  Calls 'setPositionReq' to set destination.
 *   theta is in degrees, and is measured from the home position.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * validGratingWavelength
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * validGratingWavelength(wavelength, order)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) wavelength (double)      Desired wavelength
 * (>) order (int)              Desired order
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Convert wavelength and order to angle.
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Used by EPICS to set a grating given the wavelength and order.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * validPreferredWavelength
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * validPreferredWavelength(wavelength)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) wavelength (double)      Desired wavelength
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Convert wavelength to angle.
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Determine optimal order from a table and then call 'validGratingWavelength'
 * to finish setting grating.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * setSimulation
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * setSimulation(level)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) level (int)      Simulation level desired
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Sets simulation mode
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Sets simulation mode (in gnirsG.simulation).  0 is no simulation,
 * 1 is "VSIM", 2 is FAST, and 3 is FULL.  The difference between FAST and
 * FULL is that FULL gives an approximation to the full timing but
 * always errs on the side of maximum time.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * scanStatusTask
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * scanStatusTask(a1, a2, a3, a4, a5, a6, a7, a8, a9, a10)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) a1 (int)
 * (>) a2 (int)
 * (>) a3 (int)
 * (>) a4 (int)
 * (>) a5 (int)
 * (>) a6 (int)
 * (>) a7 (int)
 * (>) a8 (int)
 * (>) a9 (int)
 * (>) a10 (int)
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Provide status information to EPICS
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * This task periodically updates memory locations from which
 * the EPICS tasks derive information for the status and alarm
 * data base.  There are two cycles: a fast one at once per second,
 * and a slow one every 5 seconds for temperature and pressure data.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
